  "question": {
    "text": "When an inorganic compound (X) having 3c-2e as well as 2c-2e bonds react with ammonia gas at a certain temperature, gives a compound (Y) isostructural with benzene. Compound (X) with ammonia at a high temperature produces a substance (Z). Which option is not correct?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "(X) is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(Z) is known as inorganic graphite",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(Y) is <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "(Z) is soft like graphite",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Diborane, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub></math> , is a compound having 3c-2e and 2c-2e bonds.<br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>B</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>6</mtext> </msub> <mtext> </mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext> </mtext><msub> <mrow> <mtext>2NH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <mtext>low</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>temp</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow> </mover> <msub> <mtext>B</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>6</mtext> </msub> <mo>⋅</mo><msub> <mrow> <mtext>2NH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <mover> <mo>→</mo> <mrow> <mtext>200</mtext><msup> <mtext> </mtext> <mtext>ο</mtext> </msup> <mtext>C</mtext></mrow> </mover> <munder> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>B</mtext> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mtext>N</mtext> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>6</mtext> </msub> </mrow> <mtext>Y</mtext> </munder> </mrow> </math><br />(Y) has structure similar to benzene. It is called inorganic benzene.<br /><math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mtext>B</mtext>   <mtext>2</mtext>  </msub>  <msub>   <mtext>H</mtext>   <mtext>6</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>NH</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>3</mtext>  </msub>  <mover>   <mo>&#x2192;</mo>   <mrow>    <mtext>high</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>temp</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow>  </mover>  <munder>   <mrow>    <msub>     <mrow>      <mtext>(BN)</mtext></mrow>     <mtext>x</mtext>    </msub>    </mrow>   <mtext>Z</mtext>  </munder>  </mrow></math>.<br />(Z) is called inorganic graphite and is a hard substance."
  }
